4. The error messages should be configurable through attributes on the directive.
5. The directive should disable the form submission button if any of the fields are invalid.
6. The directive should use ngModel or ngModelController for two-way data binding and form validation.
7. The directive should support dynamic addition and removal of input fields.
8. The form should include a password field that requires a minimum length of 8 characters and at least one uppercase letter and one number.
9. The form should include a date field that requires a specific date format (e.g., dd/mm/yyyy).
10. The form should include a dropdown field with a list of options, where at least one option must be selected.

Example usage:
<my-form
    my-required-field="true"
    my-min-length="5"
    my-max-length="10"
    my-format="email"
    my-error-message="Please enter a valid email address"
    my-submit-button-text="Submit"
    my-password-field="true"
