### Instruction:
Gather data from the web page and write a C# program to extract the page title. The program should also remove any HTML tags and extract the main content of the page.

### Response:
To extract the page title, remove HTML tags, and extract the main content of a web page in C#, you can use the following program:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        // Replace "URL" with the actual web page URL
        string url = "URL";

        // Download the web page content
        string html = DownloadWebPage(url);

        // Extract the page title
        string title = ExtractPageTitle(html);
        Console.WriteLine("Page Title: " + title);

        // Remove HTML tags and extract main content
        string mainContent = ExtractMainContent(html);
        Console.WriteLine("Main Content: " + mainContent);
    }

    static string DownloadWebPage(string url)
    {
        using (WebClient client = new WebClient())
        {
            return client.DownloadString(url);
        }
    }

    static string ExtractPageTitle(string html)
    {
        // Regex pattern to match the page title
        string pattern = @"<title>(.*?)</title>";

        // Match the pattern in the HTML
        Match match = Regex.Match(html, pattern);

        // Extract the page title
        if (match.Success)
        {
            return match.Groups[1].Value;
        }
        else
        {
            return "No page title found.";
        }
    }

    static string ExtractMainContent(string html)
    {
        // Remove HTML tags using Regex pattern
        string contentWithoutTags = Regex.Replace(html, "<.*?>", "");

        // Remove extra whitespace characters
        string trimmedContent = Regex.Replace(contentWithoutTags, @"\s+", " ");

        return trimmedContent;
    }
}
```

Replace "URL" with the actual web page URL you want to extract the data from. The program uses the `DownloadWebPage` function to download the web page content, `ExtractPageTitle` function to extract the page title using Regex, and `ExtractMainContent` function to remove HTML tags and extract the main content using Regex.

Note that this program uses the `System.Net` and `System.Text.RegularExpressions` namespaces.

### Instruction:
Using ReactJS, develop a form component that allows users to register for an event. The form should include the following input fields: Name, Age, Email, and Phone Number. The form should also include validation to ensure that the user enters a valid email address and a phone number in the format (XXX) XXX-XXXX. Additionally, the form should include a checkbox for users to agree to the event terms and conditions before submitting the form.

### Response:
Here is an example of a form component in ReactJS that allows users to register for an event with the specified input fields and validation:

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const RegisterForm = () => {
  const [name, setName] = useState('');
  const [age, setAge] = useState('');
  const [email, setEmail] = useState('');
  const [phoneNumber, setPhoneNumber] = useState('');
  const [termsChecked, setTermsChecked] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState('');

  const handleSubmit = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();

    if (!termsChecked) {
      setError('Please agree to the terms and conditions.');
      return;
    }

    // Validate email
    const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
    if (!emailRegex.test(email)) {
      setError('Please enter a valid email address.');
      return;
    }

    // Validate phone number
    const phoneRegex = /^\(\d{3}\) \d{3}-\d{4}$/;
    if (!phoneRegex.test(phoneNumber)) {
      setError('Please enter a phone number in the format (XXX) XXX-XXXX.');
      return;
    }

    // Submit the form
    // You can write your logic here to submit the form data
    console.log('Form submitted!');
    setError('');
    setName('');
    setAge('');
    setEmail('');
    setPhoneNumber('');
    setTermsChecked(false);
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
      <label>
        Name:
        <input type="text" value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} required />
      </label>
      <br />
      <label>
        Age:
        <input type="number" value={age} onChange={(e) => setAge(e.target.value)} required />
      </label>
      <br />
      <label>
        Email:
        <input type="email" value={email} onChange={(e) => setEmail(e.target.value)} required />
      </label>
      <br />
      <label>
        Phone Number:
        <input
          type="tel"
          pattern="\(\d{3}\) \d{3}-\d{4}"
          value={phoneNumber}
          onChange={(e) => setPhoneNumber(e.target.value)}
          required
        />
      </label>
      <br />
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" checked={termsChecked} onChange={(e) => setTermsChecked(e.target.checked)} required /> I agree to the terms and conditions
      </label>
      <br />
      <button type="submit">Submit</button>
      {error && <p style={{ color: 'red' }}>{error}</p>}
    </form>
  );
};

export default RegisterForm;
```

This form component includes the input fields for Name, Age, Email, and Phone Number. The email and phone number inputs have built-in validation using regular expressions to ensure the correct format is entered. The terms and conditions checkbox is required before submitting the form.

The `handleSubmit` function is called when the form is submitted. It first checks if the terms and conditions checkbox is checked. If not, it sets an error message. Then, it validates the email and phone number using regular expressions. If any validation fails, it sets an error message accordingly. If all validations pass, the form data can be submitted (you can add your own logic here).

The form component uses React hooks (useState) to manage the form data and error state. The values of the input fields are controlled by their respective state variables and updated through the `onChange` event handlers. The error message is displayed if there is an error.

You can use this `RegisterForm` component in your React application by importing and rendering it.

