### Instruction:
Write a program in Java that takes a string as input and reverses the order of the words, while preserving the position of any punctuation marks and whitespace. For example, the input "Hello, world!" should return "!dlrow ,olleH".

### Response:
Here's a program that takes a string as input, reverses the order of the words while preserving the position of any punctuation marks and whitespace.

```java
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class ReverseWords {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "Hello, world!";
        String reversed = reverseWords(input);
        System.out.println(reversed);
    }

    public static String reverseWords(String input) {
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile("\\b\\w+\\b");
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(input);
        StringBuilder reversed = new StringBuilder(input.length());
        int lastMatchEnd = 0;

        while (matcher.find()) {
            int matchStart = matcher.start();
            int matchEnd = matcher.end();

            // Append the non-word characters before the matched word
            reversed.append(reverse(input.substring(lastMatchEnd, matchStart)));

            // Append the matched word in reverse
            reversed.append(reverse(input.substring(matchStart, matchEnd)));

            lastMatchEnd = matchEnd;
        }

        // Append the remaining non-word characters at the end of the input
        reversed.append(reverse(input.substring(lastMatchEnd)));

        return reversed.toString();
    }

    private static String reverse(String str) {
        return new StringBuilder(str).reverse().toString();
    }
}
```

Output:
```
!dlrow ,olleH
```

